 number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{2}{9}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot (-63) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eea86b0-9537-5bab-868c-813e628926c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263556} {:answer/id #uuid "bd11cc58-68f3-5442-86d9-2ca462bc2de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264640} {:answer/id #uuid "c560179e-32df-53c2-bf75-91bcf107dd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264730} {:answer/id #uuid "ea98ec76-cd9c-58ef-9dd7-1b6b68c939e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265044} {:answer/id #uuid "efe386fa-5a31-5644-9aef-ffa3e5a0fe23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c560179e-32df-53c2-bf75-91bcf107dd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264730} :answer-field/id #uuid "39bcf4c6-cfb1-5621-8688-276a463c7247" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e651dd5-d08c-5af1-84eb-5024fff39147" :question/math-academy-id "q-130733" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=200.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{6}:=\\frac{3}{50}{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{50}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{3}{50}det(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{50}\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f43edac-7246-5d43-8000-c3bbff4a8176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263825} {:answer/id #uuid "86e0a75e-55d0-5e2a-9a63-a82c9c202c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264165} {:answer/id #uuid "baa05d38-6ecb-5379-9f1f-5e3e7b9ccf4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264618} {:answer/id #uuid "d4349a15-8511-5f32-95bd-1870e7829de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264848} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0308d4-84ec-5efb-85f8-99f4481efc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4349a15-8511-5f32-95bd-1870e7829de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264848} :answer-field/id #uuid "c44403e8-a5cd-5235-983a-00f2ee10a5ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "06a215a3-28a1-5081-94e6-eb4defb995c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130738" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(B)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(-2B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-2$ and $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-2B) & =(-2)^{5}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =-32\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea955b9-6711-5c65-bda1-3ab48eabd812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263132} {:answer/id #uuid "17da9e59-b9f5-509b-a7fb-62f252a7e9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263226} {:answer/id #uuid "33f0d4df-6db7-5edb-83e5-879e71782b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263453} {:answer/id #uuid "6565e424-45a3-596a-a6bd-d07a0bf5686e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263879} {:answer/id #uuid "95a19408-ad9c-5d73-b520-d5ebea3b4631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33f0d4df-6db7-5edb-83e5-879e71782b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263453} :answer-field/id #uuid "304a5032-001d-525b-8f6a-528d675f38d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d71a2d5-21fb-5641-ae6e-b88e302c6622" :question/math-academy-id "q-130739" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=2.$ What is the value of $det(-4Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-4Y) & =(-4)^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =-64\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-128.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121a0910-0c84-5231-bdd6-25a30f65897a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263167} {:answer/id #uuid "2c80c122-c6fb-5d05-9845-b09ffeb4eb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263376} {:answer/id #uuid "39934266-8c1f-5d45-a413-a141d9ef5e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263512} {:answer/id #uuid "64f7903d-1ae5-5db3-bcd2-250d5107b78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263873} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d3804a-dea0-5e00-8325-d6ee1dd1097a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c80c122-c6fb-5d05-9845-b09ffeb4eb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263376} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ae65f4-2ac2-5397-ad79-04f3366a06c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2a9423ed-dddc-5ecd-95fd-6191f18eab23" :question/math-academy-id "q-130740" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(B)=-4.$ What is the value of $det(5B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=5$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(5B) & ={5}^{2}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =25\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b73141-d30a-51a6-9f59-931d33013ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263625} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc874e1-0a0a-51b3-b460-40ba95dc7640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263673} {:answer/id #uuid "b49f38a2-031f-51dc-8877-a5a624bb1218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264552} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ac9249-0666-5a46-986f-2eafc3fc9b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264745} {:answer/id #uuid "f48bc418-eacd-5a87-a261-84a9526488c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7ac9249-0666-5a46-986f-2eafc3fc9b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264745} :answer-field/id #uuid "df63d5a1-1430-5bfe-a708-b9a8006ddea4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e4056ea9-ab56-5308-af07-58d0dddfaa0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130741" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(C)=-5,$ What is the value of $det(4C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=4$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(4C) & ={4}^{2}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0f29de-25aa-5107-8046-0dd732f9beb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263097} {:answer/id #uuid "162deb0b-2730-571d-b037-7db47a3aea46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263209} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8f75e2-26ce-5967-ac8a-f06080423598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263259} {:answer/id #uuid "66de9e61-f678-5f09-92fa-20666c0a4a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263891} {:answer/id #uuid "f578aa5a-7ba5-5a91-8942-93f38512c9ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a0f29de-25aa-5107-8046-0dd732f9beb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263097} :answer-field/id #uuid "f00b119d-2bbd-5aff-88de-546820f3c832" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da7f3dfc-3649-55d6-80af-942a6a83828d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130767" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(X)=28.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{1}$ and ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+(-7){R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{6}:={R}_{6}+(-7){R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{1}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{3}{4},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{3}{4}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we only have to multiply the determinant by $\\frac{3}{4}.$ Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =\\frac{3}{4}det(X) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c504d34-49a8-5293-9654-9bb371251af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263118} {:answer/id #uuid "668e2da3-ac3d-5bec-b6b1-16504c2d81fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263886} {:answer/id #uuid "7573103e-73e5-56e6-832d-af6582780369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264021} {:answer/id #uuid "90344634-d8cd-51fb-85d7-7f08481a8bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264236} {:answer/id #uuid "c168c56a-3c78-5c71-873d-48190da505aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90344634-d8cd-51fb-85d7-7f08481a8bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264236} :answer-field/id #uuid "37455212-8943-576e-a134-59b320488bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b71bc5d0-3557-578c-8a3d-25da59fcce16" :question/math-academy-id "q-130771" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d8f1dd-9c61-582a-91cb-1b1b14e544ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263489} {:answer/id #uuid "7cfe718c-c4c1-5e05-a605-9f1eeeec4a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264078} {:answer/id #uuid "b62d6a25-1160-5e5d-826d-11092cfa8fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264579} {:answer/id #uuid "ee61c6e2-7ebd-5d28-8d0e-3007260e4c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265084} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a2f26a-317b-5119-9e11-1fcf1b2dfd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36d8f1dd-9c61-582a-91cb-1b1b14e544ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263489} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab97c28-5a65-571d-9829-1e7bb5397bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7d54eadd-5171-5d74-9872-72cd2ba1ef45" :question/math-academy-id "q-130843" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f938576-14ee-5665-942c-f5bfc3534050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263289} {:answer/id #uuid "66e265c6-ed48-5d88-966e-a5dff8678916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263892} {:answer/id #uuid "96934c85-fbb8-5687-a238-dbee446961d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264288} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c6c16d-b28c-5665-bfd2-d38f6dbf5091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392} {:answer/id #uuid "d5476105-e8e0-591e-9f16-19d7dff3433b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3c6c16d-b28c-5665-bfd2-d38f6dbf5091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d92ecd7-28e6-5f20-bfc3-d836c30d39c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a88eab2f-0bec-591e-a119-0d1e91654bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130854" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5631a190-3164-5c81-9c22-e6a70c44c09d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263742} {:answer/id #uuid "74e1b546-dc5d-5c39-8615-b03158b816ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} {:answer/id #uuid "850ef7c7-1f4b-53c9-b078-25bda4009629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264145} {:answer/id #uuid "df7141db-3b66-5a7a-b89e-874dcb0bbee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264937} {:answer/id #uuid "e044d557-77d9-53d0-a554-77b04c1a4a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e1b546-dc5d-5c39-8615-b03158b816ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6cdcea-ffe0-5e06-a7c5-0284d3815f01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e099506-9b8a-52ad-a7eb-ff6f42b6d002" :question/math-academy-id "q-130855" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=5$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(5) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c90d582-f52e-5c66-95e3-3ad844320816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263119} {:answer/id #uuid "5e529ace-2bd8-58f0-986c-1e4d9c74356d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263816} {:answer/id #uuid "a65dd175-ee5d-5d8d-9f0d-5f2b7ace68d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264423} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4db568-3851-57c1-97bf-ea269c62e7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264629} {:answer/id #uuid "c4faeda8-6e8c-52b3-8a7f-01f15c3fc3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a65dd175-ee5d-5d8d-9f0d-5f2b7ace68d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264423} :answer-field/id #uuid "daab1c93-d290-5e33-a7b6-21310d1db988" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f6af6cd7-62fa-5e02-a671-191adf935b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130857" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=-60$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $1$st and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-60) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17febf8e-1aa5-5cbf-bf1d-e9987976f9a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263229} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdfe373-1c05-5f22-9ed5-ccf0f4dd9b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263544} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d9d6a-1705-5b61-8129-44a0f7d4d0f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264328} {:answer/id #uuid "ad82aa2b-ee84-5336-bc4d-46cbfde0facc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264491} {:answer/id #uuid "df7ef948-6ddd-520b-b34c-48ba7514f083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d9d6a-1705-5b61-8129-44a0f7d4d0f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264328} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a1e99c9-d9c5-5879-a3eb-f47e2e0715ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "527da09a-4044-5c93-b906-dff9203cb12d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130922" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3y-1,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3y-1 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04406210-94a5-519d-b563-c1787d94b573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263037} {:answer/id #uuid "20136c69-8c25-5eeb-a342-b87289d36eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263293} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd5fd9e-9a95-5bbe-b9ca-15b27ae75731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263386} {:answer/id #uuid "742c670e-1f11-5451-982a-0b676be9c761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264011} {:answer/id #uuid "b006db61-2f57-5349-bc2a-2f6efb0cae8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd5fd9e-9a95-5bbe-b9ca-15b27ae75731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263386} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff41cad-65a8-5c50-a758-f7388a3a1397" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "df63ef93-068d-5156-97ea-60671ff0c81c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130923" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ -4x+8y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f465102-c98d-5dfc-9d91-fdb16edbb2d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y-4 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263398} {:answer/id #uuid "2fe03537-fe35-52c7-80e9-18b37f436c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263404} {:answer/id #uuid "369eed24-4a3e-5e37-a6fa-62bca91eaef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263483} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9f87ff-a6c5-5cbc-997b-2e167eec652e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y+2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264222} {:answer/id #uuid "99e29834-b91b-5a2e-b900-f38024bf1f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99e29834-b91b-5a2e-b900-f38024bf1f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264318} :answer-field/id #uuid "3533a62b-3caa-5555-adaf-7ba498e1b986" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "04f20251-29bc-55e7-a2e7-4fe850dcd999" :question/math-academy-id "q-130924" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+8y &=4 \\\\ -3x+12y &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 10 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4y-2,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4y-2 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335c1d28-6ef0-501b-8648-2c0e5914f807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,6,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263444} {:answer/id #uuid "bda33206-a035-53c6-9921-6f6c110c575a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264647} {:answer/id #uuid "f4057cf8-6668-54c9-bf42-88c4d70eac10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265143} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca4d3b-5b47-5683-9882-c5ab43df0469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} {:answer/id #uuid "fda5f85f-ead2-5bc7-84eb-7f79db911497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,6,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca4d3b-5b47-5683-9882-c5ab43df0469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265178} :answer-field/id #uuid "eadf5a06-1fa1-5b76-950d-e8ed3be547ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49125958-677d-58d5-ae65-4f5b3deb04dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130926" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=-3 \\\\ y-2z &=-2 \\\\ z &=8,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=8$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-2(8)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-2+16=14.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=14$ and $z=8$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(14)+(8)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=17.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=17,y=14$, and $z=8.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨17,14,8⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543df558-b8a5-545b-b160-2fe37379c9ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} {:answer/id #uuid "c42f8e88-729f-5ad1-b070-bff1132c48a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264714} {:answer/id #uuid "c483a5fe-745e-59db-8de7-5c8a3454d240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264721} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a50c5-13c6-5393-8129-945ea4016aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb8ac6b-fce4-57dc-8d57-746bdda1d0d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263931} :answer-field/id #uuid "091832d1-1a63-50c1-8342-a7864cc522dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f61c846d-507f-5371-aeef-030ef902e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130928" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{7}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f7e074-e7a0-59f0-acfa-79c349f25b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269267} {:answer/id #uuid "017f6993-1f07-5274-a9b8-ff6a675d3954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269275} {:answer/id #uuid "aceb704a-3ddc-5fc3-8d9b-9ebd44df69c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270811} {:answer/id #uuid "d656871d-381f-5110-8839-09b5223f08da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271148} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b26bf7-07bd-54e0-b2f4-894496bc416e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d656871d-381f-5110-8839-09b5223f08da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271148} :answer-field/id #uuid "538ba8ec-40c4-591d-8b14-dd2f3bc8cc73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c934bab9-e2a5-557f-b70a-32a46819ab48" :question/math-academy-id "q-139950" :question/problem "Let $T$ be a $8\\times 8$ matrix that has $7$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{rank}(T)$ is the number of pivot columns in $T.$ \n\nSince we are told that $T$ has $7$ pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0356966e-b80c-547f-93fc-81c8d8baddc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269299} {:answer/id #uuid "2e250b53-27b4-5aae-a006-a5e9d3e734a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269683} {:answer/id #uuid "4005ee05-6e6e-5a38-9181-e2a92244bb23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269852} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d4c3c8-a1df-5063-aa90-f4150a4beda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271140} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f62bf5-cf1f-5f25-a1c7-e2626a43cce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4d4c3c8-a1df-5063-aa90-f4150a4beda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271140} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe9573b-aee4-5654-8c99-0a46fe9333a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9d3fee34-056d-53cd-a4aa-21cc533db201" :question/math-academy-id "q-139953" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $6\\times 8$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince $A$ has $8$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n8-3=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e848c5c-571a-5e64-9774-00d01483c1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269840} {:answer/id #uuid "485053f7-0cf4-5064-9d78-fece029c1309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269927} {:answer/id #uuid "6acd1ef8-2f92-53fa-839e-17421947db6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270219} {:answer/id #uuid "b35756ef-2a37-53f6-aa1c-401e085a1191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270868} {:answer/id #uuid "be5abba8-20d9-50e9-9f16-0ed198ebf305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be5abba8-20d9-50e9-9f16-0ed198ebf305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270950} :answer-field/id #uuid "90a5144d-5b7f-5cb0-877a-bcc5df428d43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8b3d88d7-df58-5328-a9cc-5e2d9def75f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-139958" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $4?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $3$  rows.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns, while the matrix $E$ has only $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=4$ and $\\text{rank}(E)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a27c8da-39a9-579c-bd39-690a5d141b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270210} {:answer/id #uuid "911eda15-9f0b-566b-bb61-5aa5ded117fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270531} {:answer/id #uuid "c79a6761-2af0-5fbd-9a09-bce6d446e1aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271027} {:answer/id #uuid "dd203548-e885-50f3-a9de-086a9a9d5137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271207} {:answer/id #uuid "f39588a0-7f73-5abb-ba4a-6821e980fca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a27c8da-39a9-579c-bd39-690a5d141b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270210} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb48c17a-a8fe-590f-8b33-3fa9a637aaee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "af7ad35e-ed21-563b-8828-398028521546" :question/math-academy-id "q-140044" :question/problem "Find $det(A)-3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero row, we obtain:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-3det(B)=0-3\\cdot 0=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1321a890-eb6a-54ac-bf48-1d4c77ff2d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269436} {:answer/id #uuid "2417ace3-b1df-55bb-9e6e-f0cf724a7d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269584} {:answer/id #uuid "445c99d0-1565-5d0f-bd0a-b81957ffc9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269889} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d5f2c0-248a-5010-b938-a0307212261a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270902} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1fdb0e-edd1-53d9-ac51-6c3cbff27cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8d5f2c0-248a-5010-b938-a0307212261a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270902} :answer-field/id #uuid "6af39b6a-785f-556e-9462-97889783ccd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "51a6e7e0-f39c-5b8c-9665-45f89b4bef77" :question/math-academy-id "q-140047" :question/problem "Find $det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|B|=-1\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-2det(B)=0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643b4a3a-7263-51ad-8b17-fdd82678cf99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464084} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e66fb8-1a18-56f4-8033-3baba4940db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "643b4a3a-7263-51ad-8b17-fdd82678cf99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464084} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ceb200f-e369-571b-b619-8f16a603488c" :answer-field/key "$A$ is a triangular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "198009c8-d9e6-556e-aa1c-228a37b12311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464086} {:answer/id #uuid "da19cf9c-0b56-5a20-b004-c70d313f5184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da19cf9c-0b56-5a20-b004-c70d313f5184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464087} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98905ac-4493-5551-96b2-6d52f8e3f566" :answer-field/key "$A$ does not have identical rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63ea76cf-d936-573e-a0be-56de7954b8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464088} {:answer/id #uuid "24e2aa19-faca-5a81-a238-e9e984e89ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24e2aa19-faca-5a81-a238-e9e984e89ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464089} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed42e6d2-1aff-5708-ad8c-b45de0195450" :answer-field/key "$A$ does not have proportional columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b81dca9a-2edb-53b6-ac28-fe026cf18a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668369} {:answer/id #uuid "e27aabb7-2b76-5680-824e-723218866528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b81dca9a-2edb-53b6-ac28-fe026cf18a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668369} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8bd4adc-5f90-5bb1-9c55-741e26d0510c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f60fdb9d-cf89-59bd-ad65-e9ec096b82df" :question/math-academy-id "q-140049" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is a triangular matrix” is false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2=5\\ne 0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ is not a triangular matrix.\n\n- Statements “$A$ does not have identical rows” and “$A$ does not have proportional columns” are true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\nHence, if $|A|\\ne 0$ then $A$ doesn't have proportional nor identical rows/columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ does not have identical rows”; “$A$ does not have proportional columns” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dcaf5cb-763f-5cf3-9460-94fc22fd63a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464090} {:answer/id #uuid "94b51605-0792-5dfb-9caa-c9f83344d279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b51605-0792-5dfb-9caa-c9f83344d279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464091} :answer-field/id #uuid "977b3534-4011-5dfd-a7b9-79927cd06b86" :answer-field/key "$A$ has proportional columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc8b5695-d93e-519e-8d9e-dc6c8a41f9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464092} {:answer/id #uuid "6b733140-0c4b-5274-8eb8-dcc1ee96785c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc8b5695-d93e-519e-8d9e-dc6c8a41f9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464092} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e5c0b84-632c-50f3-8754-70310b21a57f" :answer-field/key "$A$ has identical columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f726adc9-d1dc-521c-8654-53c52267101e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464094} {:answer/id #uuid "94789da1-7829-587f-bfab-9c55f7f2211d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f726adc9-d1dc-521c-8654-53c52267101e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464094} :answer-field/id #uuid "121070ea-b2d0-524b-8159-ea2fbac7bd33" :answer-field/key "$A$ has identical rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c152f02-0747-5d5e-81d3-22176678b033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668371} {:answer/id #uuid "270b688f-705e-5389-8d93-f675557d5a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c152f02-0747-5d5e-81d3-22176678b033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668371} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce27b83-2c2c-53a0-9721-40df10d78761" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14e63fd3-62b7-575e-b489-4cda5c20ed53" :question/math-academy-id "q-140050" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has proportional columns” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1950ae6-0473-5fe6-8e7a-228cd3690e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449732} {:answer/id #uuid "bd56d1c9-b738-5348-a8a1-732e246f1ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1950ae6-0473-5fe6-8e7a-228cd3690e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449732} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f7bc3c-eb1f-599b-8029-2012a610c8f5" :answer-field/key "$-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3864cbe3-89b6-5159-97a9-37efb82c2a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449734} {:answer/id #uuid "1fabce41-348a-50ae-8ad9-61713e395e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fabce41-348a-50ae-8ad9-61713e395e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449735} :answer-field/id #uuid "75419a8e-9154-5aff-96c8-21ca3990f7be" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d16d616a-43e7-5149-b235-d90ebb093d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449736} {:answer/id #uuid "aca33250-948f-5f9f-9edd-8103499ab8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16d616a-43e7-5149-b235-d90ebb093d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449736} :answer-field/id #uuid "44699a4d-8bdd-5ddc-ac60-498b82a1f309" :answer-field/key "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8e786624-3795-5bd2-9044-40e13fec09b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-157162" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =-2\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b32cae0a-cfa4-5a48-bec0-bec8d7dc3e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449738} {:answer/id #uuid "6d898115-c0eb-5d34-a917-b7dcf7a96360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b32cae0a-cfa4-5a48-bec0-bec8d7dc3e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449738