67-515c-a6d4-f4d315e78809" :question/math-academy-id "q-157238" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-8+6 \\\\ -1+10-9 \\\\ 7+2-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false. Since statement ${a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=1,\\,{x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b